{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.WedderburnArtin","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.IsAlgClosed","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Pi","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Projection","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finrank","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.Finite.Matrix","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Equiv","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Pi","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtClassification","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyOV","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Bilinear"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.snBlocks_c2_aligned","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.snBlocks_c2_aligned","kind":"theorem","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L454-L490","doc":"**The aligned isotypic projection family + `C₂` eigen-decomposition (the capstone core), now\nsorry-free modulo the single isotypic split `sn_isotypic_specht_split`.** Over a characteristic-zero\nfield `R`, a partition-indexed family `proj i` onto blocks `p i` that is the `snBlocks` bundle\n(`IsProj`, ranks `(dim S^{λ_i})²`, `∑ proj = id`) **and** block-diagonalises the central JM element:\n`mulLeft C₂ = ∑ i, contentSqSum λ_i • proj i`.\n\nThe projection family is `transProj e i` for the isotypic `e` from `sn_isotypic_specht_split`;\nconjuncts 1–3 reuse the sorry-free `transProj_isProj` / `finrank_range_transProj` / `transProj_sum`,\nand conjunct 4 (the `C₂` block-diagonalisation) is the sorry-free `mulLeft_eq_sum_transProj` applied to\nthe core's carried-`C₂` clause.  The entire `C₂`-decomposition machinery is thus discharged sorry-free;\nonly the isotypic split itself remains cited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.mulLeft_eq_sum_transProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.mulLeft_eq_sum_transProj","kind":"theorem","line":423,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L423-L446","doc":"**The `mulLeft`-conjugation payoff (sorry-free).** If an algebra iso `e : A ≃ₐ ∏ⱼ Bⱼ` carries a\ncentral element `z` to a block-scalar `fun i => γ i • 1`, then `mulLeft z` block-diagonalises:\n`mulLeft z = ∑ᵢ γ i • transProj e.toLinearEquiv i`.  Conjugate `mulLeft` by `e` (algebra-hom\nproperty), apply `mulLeft_blockScalar`, push the composition through the finite sum/scalar.  No\ncenter-of-product lemma is required — the block-scalar shape is the hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.mulLeft_blockScalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.mulLeft_blockScalar","kind":"theorem","line":398,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L398-L414","doc":"On the product algebra `∏ⱼ Bⱼ`, left-multiplication by a **block-scalar** element\n`fun i => γ i • 1` equals `∑ᵢ γ i • coordProj i`: on coordinate `i` it scales by `γ i`. Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.freeProjClaim_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.freeProjClaim_false","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L370-L384","doc":"**The free-`proj` decomposition is FALSE** (machine-proved, no `sorry`).  At `n = 2` over `ℚ`,\ninstantiating at `proj ≡ 0` forces `mulLeft C₂ = 0`, hence (apply to `1`) `C₂ = 0`, contradicting\n`C₂(1) = binom(2,2) = 1`.  Hence the `decomp` block-diagonalisation holds only for the *aligned*\nisotypic family of `snBlocks_c2_aligned` below, not for an arbitrary `proj`.  Axioms\n`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.FreeProjClaim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.FreeProjClaim","kind":"def","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L361-L368","doc":"The free-`proj` decomposition predicate: `mulLeft C₂ = ∑ i, contentSqSum λ_i • proj i` for an\n**unconstrained** `proj`.  (The `decomp` field of `SnWedderburnSpectralData` is this equation for a\n*specific aligned* `proj` — never a free one; see `freeProjClaim_false`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.snBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.snBridge","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L327-L346","doc":"**THE BRIDGE.** The partition-indexed isotypic projection family of `R[S_n]` over a\ncharacteristic-zero field `R`: projections `proj i` onto blocks `p i` of `R`-dimension\n`(dim S^{λ_i})²`, summing to the identity. Stated **exactly** as `OVTopAssembly.snBlocks`, so that\nthe capstone can replace its opaque cited `sorry` by `exact … snBridge n`.\n\n**Sorry-free modulo the one named core** `sn_rational_specht_split` (the rational + OV-labelled\nsplit): that split is fed to the sorry-free mechanical extraction `snBlocks_of_algEquiv`, whose\n`finrank` output `(dim S^{λ_i})²` is already the `snBlocks` block size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.snBlocks_of_algEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.snBlocks_of_algEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L293-L323","doc":"**The full `snBlocks` bundle from an algebra `∏ Matrix` decomposition (sorry-free).** Given *any*\n`R`-algebra isomorphism `e : R[S_n] ≃ₐ[R] ∏_{i:PartitionIndex n} Matrix(Fin dᵢ) R`, the coordinate\nidempotents pulled back along `e` form a complete family of projections onto blocks of `R`-dimension\n`dᵢ²`. This is the entire content of `OVTopAssembly.snBlocks` *except* the choice of `e` (with\n`dᵢ = dim S^{λ_i}`) — i.e. the bulk of the gap, discharged by pure linear algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.sn_rational_specht_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.sn_rational_specht_split","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L275-L289","doc":"**Rational Wedderburn split — a corollary of the isotypic core.** Over a characteristic-zero\nfield `R`, the rational, OV-labelled Wedderburn decomposition of `R[S_n]`, indexed by the partitions\nof `n`, with block `i` of matrix size exactly `dim_R S^{λ_i}`:\n`R[S_n] ≃ₐ[R] ∏_{i:PartitionIndex n} Matrix(Fin (dim S^{λ_i})) R`.\n\n**Sorry-free modulo the single core** `sn_isotypic_specht_split`: forgetting that theorem's\ncarried-`C₂` clause yields exactly this algebra iso (same `e`).  The isotypic split is strictly\nstronger, so the previous shape's two independent cited cores collapse to one.\n`-- Ref: [james1984representation], [sagan2001]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.sn_isotypic_specht_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.sn_isotypic_specht_split","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L263-L273","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.SnIsotypicSpechtSplit.exists_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.SnIsotypicSpechtSplit.exists_split","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L252-L252","doc":"Mathlib lacks char-0 rationality (Maschke) for S_n, Specht module alignment, and the isotypic/C₂ block alignment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.SnIsotypicSpechtSplit.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.SnIsotypicSpechtSplit.mk","kind":"ctor","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L250-L250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.SnIsotypicSpechtSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.SnIsotypicSpechtSplit","kind":"class","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L231-L261","doc":"**Named core (the genuine isotypic-aligned `S_n`-rep-theory gap).** Over a characteristic-zero\nfield `R`, a *rational, OV-labelled* Wedderburn algebra isomorphism\n`R[S_n] ≃ₐ[R] ∏_{i:PartitionIndex n} Matrix(Fin (dim S^{λ_i})) R` with block `i` the\n`S^{λ_i}`-**isotypic** component, **carrying** the central Jucys–Murphy element `C₂ = Σ_k X_k²` to the\nblock-scalar family `fun i => contentSqSum λ_i • 1`.\n\nThe carried-`C₂` clause *is* the isotypic alignment, made operational: by\n`JucysMurphy.centralC2_acts_by_contentSqSum`, `C₂` acts on the `S^{λ_i}`-isotypic block by\n`contentSqSum λ_i` (Schur per isotypic component), so an `e` whose block `i` *is* that component sends\n`C₂` to `contentSqSum λ_i • 1` there.  Conversely the clause **forces** the alignment (a size-aligned\nsplit need not be isotypic; `freeProjClaim_false` shows an unconstrained `proj` cannot satisfy the\ndecomposition), so bundling it into the existential is the honest, non-over-general disposition.\nThis is the **single** named core of the file: the plain rational split\n`sn_rational_specht_split` is derived from it, and §5's `snBlocks_c2_aligned` consumes it directly.\nMathlib (pinned v4.24.0) lacks every piece this folds in: ℚ-rationality (collapsing division rings\nto `R`; it has the matrix product only over an algebraically closed base), the partition labelling,\nthe OV identification block `i` ↔ `S^{λ_i}` of size `dim_R S^{λ_i}`, and the isotypic /\n`C₂`-eigenvalue alignment.\n`-- Ref: [vershik-kerov1977], [sagan2001], [james1984representation]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.finrank_range_transProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.finrank_range_transProj","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L207-L217","doc":"**The `R`-dimension of the `i`-th pulled-back block** equals `finrank R (B i)`: conjugation by a\nlinear equiv preserves rank, and the coordinate-block range is `≃ₗ B i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.transProj_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.transProj_sum","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L194-L205","doc":"The pulled-back projections **sum to the identity** (the blocks exhaust `A`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.transProj_isProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.transProj_isProj","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L187-L192","doc":"The pulled-back idempotent is a **projection** onto its range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.transProj_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.transProj_idem","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L180-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.transProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.transProj","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L176-L178","doc":"**The pulled-back idempotent** `e.symm ∘ coordProj i ∘ e : A →ₗ[R] A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.finrank_range_coordProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.finrank_range_coordProj","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L172-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.single_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.single_inj","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L159-L163","doc":"`LinearMap.single R B i` is injective (it is a section of `proj i`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.range_coordProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.range_coordProj","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L149-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.coordProj_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.coordProj_sum","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L146-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.coordProj_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.coordProj_idem","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L141-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.coordProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.coordProj","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.lean#L137-L139","doc":"The `i`-th **coordinate idempotent** on `∏ⱼ Bⱼ`: zero out every coordinate but `i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}